<% content_for :title, "Library folder — Tinkerex" %>

<%# WHICH FOLDER IS THE LIBRARY (K, 2026-10-20). ONE TEMPLATE FOR ALL THREE STATES -- pending (the
    first-run confirmation), chosen (the change form), and a backend with no folder -- so the template
    sweep (template_hygiene_test.rb) renders it on every backend leg. The form is the same in both
    share states: shared/_folder_field over Settings::LibraryController#children, with no create_url
    (a folder is made on the host, not here), writing the path relative to the mount into `relative`.

    THE ACCENT IS SPENT ONCE (design-system.md rule 13): "Use this folder", or with a catalog to keep
    "Switch to this folder". "Start over" is a quiet button behind a confirmation that says what it
    forgets and that nothing on disk is touched, because "start over" otherwise reads as "delete".

    ONLY AN ADMIN GETS THE FORM (2026-10-21, Settings::LibraryController's header). Every other account
    reads the same page with no form and no chooser: the folder, its file count and its alerts, each
    alert's next step handed to an admin, and one sentence saying an admin changes it. %>
<%# The Settings breadcrumb, except on first run: until the folder is confirmed every page brings
    the maker back here, so a link to Settings would only bounce, and the top bar shows the title. %>
<%= render "settings/crumbs", current: "Library folder" unless @pending %>

<div class="page-head">
  <h1>Library folder</h1>
</div>

<% if @error %>
  <div class="form-errors flash-alert" role="alert"><%= @error %></div>
<% end %>

<% if !@share %>
  <%= render "shared/where_files_come_from", projects: false %>
  <p class="muted">There is no folder to choose for this library.</p>
<% else %>
  <% if @pending && !@can_change %>
    <p>This server's library folder has not been chosen yet.</p>
  <% elsif @pending %>
    <p>Your library will be <strong><%= library_folder_label %></strong>.</p>
    <ul class="library-facts">
      <li>It is scanned now and every 15 minutes, and whatever another program puts there appears here.</li>
      <li>Uploads in the browser land in it, as ordinary files.</li>
      <li>Deleting in the app moves a file into its <code>.trash/</code> folder, never off the disk.</li>
    </ul>
  <% else %>
    <p>Your library is <strong><%= library_root_label(@relative) %></strong>,
      with <%= pluralize(@file_count, "file") %> scanned.</p>
    <% if @root_missing %>
      <div class="form-errors flash-alert" role="alert">That folder is not there any more, so nothing
        in it can be read.
        <% if @can_change %>Put it back on the host, or choose again below.<% else %>An admin can put it
          back on the host or choose another here.<% end %></div>
    <% end %>
    <%# THE REFUSAL IN A MAKER'S WORDS (UX audit F8). library_scan_refusal holds the scan's raw
        message, written for the failed-jobs row; Settings::LibraryController#refusal_counts reads the
        numbers out of it, and the message itself never prints. The variable may: this is the page an
        admin changes the folder on, and the limit is theirs to raise. %>
    <% if @refusal.present? %>
      <div class="form-errors flash-alert" role="alert">
        <% if (counts = @refusal_counts) %>
          The last scan stopped because it would have removed <%= counts[:doomed] %> of
          <%= counts[:total] %> files from the catalog, more than the <%= counts[:limit] %>% one scan
          may remove. Check that the folder is mounted and holds your files, then rescan.
          <% if @can_change %>If the files really are gone, raise the limit in
            <code>LIBRARY_SCAN_MAX_DELETE_PCT</code>; if the folder holds a different set of files,
            choose it again with <strong>Start over</strong>.<% else %>An admin can raise the limit or
            choose the folder again here.<% end %>
        <% else %>
          The last scan of this folder stopped before it changed anything.
          <% if @can_change %>If the folder holds a different set of files, choose it again with
            <strong>Start over</strong>; otherwise choose the folder that holds your files.<% else %>An
            admin can choose the folder again here.<% end %>
        <% end %>
      </div>
    <% end %>
    <%# THE SCANNING NOTE, the Rescan reload's own element and rules (files/index.html.erb):
        rendered only on the redirect after a change, pointed at this page WITHOUT ?scanning=1 so the
        reloaded page polls nothing, and carrying the stamp this render read. %>
    <% if params[:scanning] == "1" %>
      <p class="muted">Scanning the library…
        <span data-controller="scanreload"
              data-scanreload-url-value="<%= settings_library_path %>"
              data-scanreload-status-url-value="<%= scan_status_files_path %>"
              data-scanreload-since-value="<%= current_user.library_scanned_stamp %>"></span></p>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>

  <% if !@can_change %>
    <p class="muted">
      <% if @pending %>
        An admin chooses the library folder for every user on this server. Until one does, every
        page brings you back here.
      <% else %>
        An admin changes the library folder, for every user on this server.
      <% end %>
    </p>
  <% else %>
    <%= form_with url: settings_library_path, method: :patch, class: "settings-add library-choice" do %>
      <%= render "shared/folder_field",
                 name: "relative",
                 children_url: children_settings_library_path,
                 value: @relative.to_s,
                 root_label: library_folder_text,
                 label: if @pending then "Choose a folder inside it"
                        elsif @relative.present? then "/#{@relative}"
                        else library_folder_text
                        end %>
      <% if @pending || @catalog_empty %>
        <button type="submit" class="btn primary">Use this folder</button>
      <% else %>
        <ul class="library-outcomes">
          <li><strong>Switch to this folder</strong> keeps each file's projects, notes and tags when it
            holds the same files, moved or renamed. If it holds different files, the scan refuses and
            says so here.</li>
          <li><strong>Start over with this folder</strong> forgets the files scanned so far and scans
            this folder fresh. Nothing on disk is deleted or moved.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="library-actions">
          <button type="submit" class="btn primary">Switch to this folder</button>
          <button type="submit" name="start_over" value="1" class="btn"
                  data-turbo-confirm="Start over? Tinkerex forgets every file it has scanned, with their previews, notes, pins and the 3D models it found, and scans this folder fresh. Your projects, tasks, inventory and BOMs stay, and each project keeps its folder when this one has a folder at the same path. Nothing is deleted from disk: the old folder and its files are untouched.">Start over with this folder</button>
        </div>
      <% end %>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>

  <% if @pending && @can_change %>
    <p class="muted">To choose from a wider folder, set <code>LIBRARY_HOST_PATH</code> in the
      <code>.env</code> beside your <code>docker-compose.yml</code> to it and run
      <code>docker compose up -d</code> again. <%= link_to "Help", help_path %> says more.</p>
  <% end %>
<% end %>
